              "role": "mechanism",
              "text": "A single-cell reference uses column letter then row number: B2. A rectangular range uses a start address, a colon, and an end address: A10:E20 covers columns A through E, rows 10 through 20. A whole-column reference repeats the letter: B:B covers every cell in column B. A formula picks the form that matches how many cells it needs.",
